  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development must be carried out in accordance with the recommendations of the Flood Risk Assement received 11th September 2025 unless otherwise approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The works that must be carried out are:\r\n\r\n1) Flood Resilient Construction:  Electrical sockets shall be installed at raised levels above finished floor height. Wiring systems shall be designed to reduce flood damage risk.\r\n2) Finished Floor Levels: The extension’s finished floor level shall match the existing dwelling’s floor level to maintain continuity and avoid unnecessary elevation.\r\n3) Sustainable Drainage System (SuDS): A water butt with a minimum capacity of 210 litres shall be installed to collect rainwater from roof drainage.\r\nThe water butt shall include a tap, lid, stand, and downpipe diverter kit.\r\n4) Maintenance: The water butt and associated drainage components shall be maintained in accordance with the schedule outlined in the FRA, including annual inspections and post-storm checks.\r\n\r\nReason: To ensure the development is resilient to flood risk and does not increase flood risk elsewhere, in accordance with the National Planning Policy Framework and local flood risk guidance."
  ],
